  "scope": "For any fixed exterior whose composition with the actual twenty-vertex shared-tip disk is a spherical cubic connected bridgeless map, replacing that disk by its ordered eight-cycle preserves this class, removes twelve vertices and reconstructs an original colouring from every supplied smaller-map colouring. No extra exterior-connectivity or Kempe-closure hypothesis is needed. A closed reference hub observation supplies successful choices; its readback preserves the entire ordered trace and genuine exterior witnesses.",
  "limits": "The auxiliary hub is quasicubic with an eight-valent vertex, not the cubic induction map. Reconstruction may recolour the exterior and retains configuration 6 and generic checker support. Geometry and transport exclude all configuration certificates. The proof does not establish closure of all physical exterior traces, extract executable Kempe histories, preserve colouring counts, recognize the disk in an arbitrary source, or establish coverage. It adds no complete-assembly certificate replacement or catalogue reduction.",
  "remaining": "Construct an actual vertex-side occurrence consumer using exact source dart/vertex transport; then derive useful face-pattern recognition and geometric supply. Preserve the retained-base versus uniform-family distinction."
